# Multi-Model Routing

**Applies when:** the kit is configured in `multi-model` mode (set by `ai-resources setup`).

## Architecture

```
Claude Code / Aider  (the cockpits the kit points at a gateway; multi-model only)
    │  ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL (Claude Code) · OpenAI-compatible base (Aider)
    ▼
Gateway: LiteLLM (local) or OpenRouter (hosted)
    │  inspects {"model": "..."} field
    ▼
Provider (Anthropic / Google / OpenAI / DeepSeek / Moonshot / Vertex / Ollama)
```

Every other cockpit (Cursor, Gemini CLI, Codex, Copilot, Windsurf, Continue, OpenCode) keeps its own model
settings: the kit writes instructions and MCP for it and claims nothing about routing. Gemini CLI also gets its
auth setting. OpenClaw runs its own engines (`claude-code`, `codex`, `antigravity`); Antigravity uses agy's own
model ids, never an API id.

The authoritative table (cockpit x provider x mode, every cell cited to the code) is
`scripts/ai_resources/setup/compat.py`, rendered in `docs/multi-model.md`. A cell that is not verified end to
end behaves as "skip" unless the user passes `--allow-unverified`.

For the cockpits that are wired to a gateway, the HTTP calls hit it at the configured `gateway.url` (default
`127.0.0.1:4000`). LiteLLM reads the `model` field from each request and routes to the matching provider,
translating between API formats as needed.

## Single source of truth: `~/.config/ai-resources/executors.yaml`

```yaml
version: 1
profile_name: unified-default
gateway:
  url: http://127.0.0.1:4000
  api_key_env: LITELLM_MASTER_KEY
by_role:
  research:           { provider: google,    model: gemini-3.8-flash }
  planner:            { provider: anthropic, model: claude-sonnet-5 }
  software-architect: { provider: anthropic, model: claude-opus-5 }
  implementer:        { provider: anthropic, model: claude-sonnet-5 }
  ...
```

Each role's `model` value is sent **verbatim** to the gateway. To change which
model runs a role, edit this file and re-run `ai-resources setup` (or run
`ai-resources daemon restart` if only the gateway config changed).

## How subagents inherit models

In Claude Code, subagent files at `~/.claude/agents/<role>.md` declare:

```yaml
---
name: research
description: ...
model: gemini-3.8-flash    # ← string passes through to the gateway (Claude Code, multi-model)
tools: Read, Grep, Glob
---
```

In multi-model mode Claude Code forwards the `model:` value to the gateway without
checking it against an Anthropic allowlist, so a string the gateway recognizes
reaches it. Whether a given non-Claude model works end to end through Claude Code
is a matrix cell (`compat.py`), and an unverified cell is not configured by
default. In single-model mode (no gateway) Claude Code runs only Claude models
and a non-Claude id is never written.

For other cockpits the kit writes no model setting, except Aider's
`architect-model` / `model` / `weak-model` (in `~/.aider.conf.yml`, multi-model
only, with the gateway's OpenAI-compatible base) and OpenClaw's engine model.

## What works cross-provider

- ✅ **Tools** (Read, Write, Bash, Grep, Edit) — Claude Code executes locally;
  only the model's tool-use call format is translated by LiteLLM.
- ✅ **MCP servers** (Engram, etc.) — appear as standard tools to the model;
  format-translated by LiteLLM.
- ✅ **Skills** — text injected into context; agnostic to provider.
- ✅ **Workspace access** — same as native Claude Code.
- ✅ **Workflow YAML iteration** — orchestrator behavior unchanged.

## What does NOT work cross-provider

- ❌ **Anthropic prompt caching** — `cache_control` headers are Anthropic-only.
  When routing to Gemini/OpenAI, caching is lost (Gemini and OpenAI have their
  own caching, format-specific).
- ❌ **Anthropic-only beta features** — computer-use, code-execution betas,
  citations. Use Claude models for subagents that depend on these.
- ⚠️ **Edge-case translation** — parallel tool calls, complex JSON Schema
  with refs/oneOf, streaming + tools may have variance. Most basic flows work.

## Single source for cost / observability

LiteLLM logs every call. Use:

- `ai-resources daemon logs` — raw logs
- `ai-resources audit` — cost breakdown per role/model
- `ai-resources executors test <role>` — round-trip a single role

## When mode is `single-model`

Multi-model routing is bypassed. The cockpit talks directly to its native
provider (e.g. Claude Code → Anthropic) and `executors.yaml` is not used.
Subagent `model:` values come from a single-model profile chosen in setup:
`claude-native` (Claude aliases per role) or `claude-inherit` (every role
inherits the session model).

## Health check

Run `ai-resources doctor` to verify:
- LiteLLM gateway is reachable
- Each configured model accepts a tiny round-trip
- All credentials are loaded
- Cockpits are configured

## Delegation and cost

Routing changes which model runs a role; it does not change when to delegate.
Delegate by task shape (skill `kit-orchestration`): context-heavy work,
independent review, parallel fan-out. Targeted reads and small edits stay in
the main session — every spawned subagent re-sends its system prompt and
tools, and a route that loses prompt caching can cost more than a cached
Claude call. Keep verification, review and security on strong models.

## Relation to other rules

- Skill `kit-orchestration` — workflow iteration is unchanged; only the model
  behind each subagent changes.
- `200-security-mcp.mdc` — credentials in `~/.config/ai-resources/.env`
  (chmod 600); never committed; `${env:VAR}` references in YAML.
